<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuryev-Polsky</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuryev-Polsky is a small town in Vladimir Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuri-dolgoruky">Yuri Dolgoruky</a> founded it in 1152 in the open fields, polye, between Vladimir and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pereslavl-zalessky">Pereslavl-Zalessky</a>, and from 1212 it was the seat of a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> principality. It is known for the Cathedral of Saint George, built in 1230 to 1234 and covered with carved stone reliefs.</p></div>
